course: dictionary
lesson: 7936
title: A word with many realms
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A realm is a land ruled by a king or queen, which means a kingdom. Old and formal writing often uses it this way. «The British monarch is also head of state of 14 other Commonwealth countries, such as Australia, Canada, New Zealand and Jamaica, which are called Commonwealth realms.» Here a realm is a country that has a king or queen as its head of state.
explain: Realm can also mean an area of knowledge or activity. In «the realm of science», the word means the whole world of science, everything that belongs to it. Ask yourself what is being talked about, then the word tells you the area.
explain: In stories, a realm is a world or land, often a magical one. Fairy tales and fantasy books are full of them. If you see castles, magic or fairies near the word, that is a clue that the realm is a land of its own.
explain: Look at the phrases too. «Within the realms of possibility» means something that could really happen. The words around realm show you which meaning fits, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Realm is a noun, and its plural is realms.
fact: «Realm» means a kingdom, or a country ruled by a king or queen.
fact: «Realm» can mean an area of knowledge or activity, as in «the realm of science».
fact: «Realm» can mean a magical world or land, as in «the realm of the fairies».
fact: «Within the realms of possibility» means something that could really happen.
exercise: In «The British monarch is also head of state of 14 other Commonwealth countries, which are called Commonwealth realms», what is a realm? | A kind of fruit | A type of cloud | *A country with a king or queen as head of state | A room in a castle
exercise: Ella reads, «She studied the realm of science for years.» What does realm mean here? | *An area of knowledge or interest | A kind of loud storm | A sudden shout | A small dark room
exercise: Find and copy the word in «The fairies lived in a magical realm beyond the mountains» that means a world or land. | mountains | beyond | *realm | magical
test:
In «the realm of the fairies», what does realm mean? | A shiny metal | *A magical world or land | A type of bird | A long, boring lesson
What does «within the realms of possibility» mean? | Something impossible and silly | *Something that could really happen | A list of kingdoms on a map | Something that happened long ago
exam: Which meaning of realm fits «the realm of science»? | *An area of knowledge or activity | A magical land of dragons | A kingdom ruled by a king | A knight's sword
